Fellow gamers,
  Your humble moderator screwed up when batching up the recent umoria3
posting - as many of you have reported. The major problem was that I
didn't realize that Mac .hqx files often (always?) don't have trailing
newlines, thus confusing the shar program. Also, while trying to hand
fit some of the large files into files for posting, the directory
info was lost and several files got lost.
  Here is what you need to do:
	1) edit Part06, Part09, Part24, Part26, Part28 and Part30.
	   Wherever the string "END_OF_FILE" appears at the end of
	   a file, but not at the begining of a line, insert a newline.
	   Add 1 to the word count in the next line (optional - if you
	   don't do this, ignore the warning about being unpacked with
	   the wrong count).
	   This occurs with all of the .hqx files and "files/origcmds.hlp".

	2) the files: misc2.c, moria1.c, moria2.c and spells.c got
	   unpacked in the top level directory. mv them to the "source"
	   directory.

	3) grab Part32/31 (to be posted to c.s.g. shortly). It has the
	   missing files, along with a uuencoded copy of "mac/scrnmgr/ScrnMgr.doc"
	   (it had many long lines that got munged by mailers) and an
	   updated MANIFEST.

  Sorry for the problems and hassles. Next time I promise I'll be more
careful :-).

